\================================================================================ CYTRON ROBO PICO DATASHEET (FULL EXTRACTION) Simplifying Robotics with Raspberry Pi Pico / Pico W ================================================================================ Document Info: Datasheet Rev 1.0 (April 2023) Manufacturer: Cytron Technologies Inc. / Cytron Technologies Sdn Bhd Website: www.cytron.io | Support: support@cytron.io | Sales: sales@cytron.io Address: No. 1, Lorong Industri Impian 1, Taman Industri Impian, 14000 Bukit Mertajam, Penang, Malaysia. Tel: +604 - 548 0668 | Fax: +604 - 548 0669 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 1\. BOARD LAYOUT &amp; FUNCTION DESCRIPTIONS -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- • VIN TERMINAL: - Connect to any DC power source within 3.6V to 6.0V range. - Screw terminal connector. • LIPO BATTERY CONNECTOR: - Connect to a single-cell LiPo / Li-Ion battery via JST PH2.0 connector. - Battery is rechargeable directly via the USB port on the Pico / Pico W. - Integrated battery protection against overcharge and overdischarge. - Note: If board does not turn on with battery connected, connect USB to charge and reset protection circuit. • POWER LED: - Red LED, turns ON when board power is active. • ON/OFF SWITCH: - Physical slide switch to turn board power ON/OFF (including Pico power). • RESET BUTTON: - Pushbutton to reset the Raspberry Pi Pico or Pico W. • PI PICO SOCKET: - Dual female pin header sockets for mounting Raspberry Pi Pico or Pico W. • GPIO BREAKOUT (FEMALE PIN HEADERS): - Complete breakout of all Raspberry Pi Pico / Pico W GPIO pins alongside Pico socket. • GROVE PORTS (7 PORTS): - Port 1: GP0 (PWM0-A, SDI0, SDA0, TX0) | GP1 (PWM0-B, CSn0, SCL0, RX0) - Port 2: GP2 (PWM1-A, SCK0, SDA1) | GP3 (PWM1-B, SDO0, SCL1) - Port 3: GP4 (PWM2-A, SDI0, SDA0, TX1) | GP5 (PWM2-B, CSn0, SCL0, RX1) - Port 4: GP16 (PWM0-A, SDI0, SDA0, TX0) | GP17 (PWM0-B, CSn0, SCL0, RX0) - Port 5: GP6 (PWM3-A, SCK0, SDA1) | GP26 (PWM5-A, SDA1, ADC0) - Port 6: GP26 (PWM5-A, SDA1, ADC0) | GP27 (PWM5-B, SCL1, ADC1) - Port 7: GP7 (PWM3-B, SDO0, SCL1) | GP28 (PWM6-A, ADC2) • MAKER PORT: - Compatible with Qwiic / Stemma QT / Grove modules (with conversion cable). - Pins are shared directly with Grove 2 Port (GP2, GP3). • NEOPIXEL RGB LED: - User-programmable WS2812 RGB LED connected to GP18\. • PROGRAMMABLE BUTTONS: - 2x user pushbuttons accessible from firmware programs: - Button 1: Connected to GP20 - Button 2: Connected to GP21 • PIEZO BUZZER: - Onboard piezo buzzer connected to GP22 for audio tone/melody generation. - Includes physical Buzzer Mute Switch to silence sound. • GPIO STATUS LEDS: - 12x Blue status indicator LEDs for Pico GPIOs mapped to Grove ports. - LEDs turn ON whenever the corresponding GPIO pin logic state is HIGH. • MOTOR TEST BUTTONS: - Instant hardware test buttons to drive motor channels at 100% duty cycle: - M1A / M2A: Forward rotation - M1B / M2B: Reverse/Backward rotation • SERVO PORTS: - 3-pin headers for 4x RC Servo Motors: - Servo 1: GP12 - Servo 2: GP13 - Servo 3: GP14 - Servo 4: GP15 - Servo power supply (V+) is equal to the main power source input voltage. • MOTOR STATUS LEDS: - Visual status LEDs for DC motor channels (turn ON during motor operation): - M1A / M2A: Forward indicator - M1B / M2B: Reverse indicator • DC MOTOR TERMINALS: - 2x 2-pin screw terminals for dual DC motor channels: - Motor Channel 1 (M1): GP8 (M1A) and GP9 (M1B) - Motor Channel 2 (M2): GP10 (M2A) and GP11 (M2B) - Full speed motor voltage equals the power input voltage. - Reversing MxA and MxB connections reverses physical motor rotation direction. • VBAT SENSE JUMPER: - Solder jumper on bottom side of board allowing battery/input voltage measurement. - Connects to GP28 / ADC2 through a 1/2 voltage divider: V\_ADC2 = VBAT / 2 (where VBAT is highest of VIN, VUSB, or VLiPo). -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 2\. TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS &amp; ABSOLUTE MAXIMUM RATINGS -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- • Power Input Voltage (USB, LiPo, or VIN): 3.6V (Min) to 6.0V (Max) • Digital Input Voltage Low Level: -0.3V to 0.8V • Digital Input Voltage High Level: 2.0V to 3.6V • Digital Output Voltage Low Level: 0V to 0.5V • Digital Output Voltage High Level: 2.6V to 3.3V • Analog Input Voltage Range: 0V to 3.3V • Vmotor &amp; Vservo Output Voltage: - Only USB Connected: VUSB - 0.4V - Only LiPo or VIN Connected: VLiPo or VIN - USB + LiPo Connected: VUSB - 0.4V - USB + VIN Connected (VIN &lt; VUSB): VUSB - 0.4V - USB + VIN Connected (VIN &gt; VUSB, VIN - VUSB &lt; 0.6V): VIN - 0.4V - USB + VIN Connected (VIN - VUSB &gt; 0.6V): VIN • Maximum DC Motor Current (Per Channel): - Continuous Current: 1.0 A - Peak Current (&lt; 5 seconds): 1.5 A • DC Motor Driver Max PWM Frequency: 20 kHz • Total +3V3 Output Current (Grove Ports): 300 mA Max • Operating Temperature Range: -20°C to +85°C -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 3\. MOTOR DRIVER TRUTH TABLE -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | Input A (GP8 / GP10) | Input B (GP9 / GP11) | Output A (M1A / M2A) | Output B (M1B / M2B) | Motor Action | |----------------------|----------------------|----------------------|----------------------|--------------| | Low | Low | Low | Low | Brake | | High | Low | High | Low | Forward | | Low | High | Low | High | Backward | | High | High | Hi-Z (Open) | Hi-Z (Open) | Coast | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 4\. PHYSICAL DIMENSIONS -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- • Overall Board Size: 88.0 mm x 72.0 mm • Mounting Hole Spacing (Outer): 82.0 mm x 58.0 mm • Mounting Hole Spacing (Inner): 80.0 mm x 48.0 mm • Mounting Hole Diameter: 4x 3.0 mm (Ø 3mm) • Board Corner Radius / Feature: Ø 4.8 mm -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 5\. POWER TREE &amp; ARCHITECTURE -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- • Power Inputs: 1\. VIN (Terminal Block, 3.6V - 6.0V) 2\. VUSB (Micro USB from Pico/Pico W) 3\. VBAT (Single Cell LiPo via JST PH2.0) • Multiple Power Input Selector: Automatically selects the highest voltage source. • Charging Circuitry: USB power feeds onboard Battery Charging IC to recharge LiPo. • Motor &amp; Servo Power Rail: Direct power feed from Input Selector (no voltage regulation). • Onboard Power Regulation: - Buck-Boost Converter supplies regulated +3V3 rail (up to 800 mA). - +3V3 Rail powers Pico / Pico W, Grove / Maker Ports, Piezo Buzzer, WS2812 NeoPixel, and 13x Status LEDs. ================================================================================